# ============================================================
# Lakenzie's Site — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (same folder — the repo root) and
# fill in real values. The backend loads `.env` FROM THE REPO
# ROOT via pydantic-settings, so keep it here, not in backend\.
#
# `.env` is gitignored; this example file is the documentation.
# ============================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL — SQLAlchemy connection string for SQL Server.
#
# Optional for now: the site runs without a database until the
# games feature is wired up. Leave unset and the backend will
# simply skip DB access.
#
# Example 1 — SQL auth (username/password):
# DATABASE_URL=mssql+pyodbc://user:pass@localhost/lakenzie_games?driver=ODBC+Driver+18+for+SQL+Server&TrustServerCertificate=yes
#
# Example 2 — Windows auth (no password; uses your logged-in user):
# DATABASE_URL=mssql+pyodbc://@localhost/lakenzie_games?driver=ODBC+Driver+18+for+SQL+Server&TrustServerCertificate=yes&trusted_connection=yes
#
# Notes:
# - "ODBC+Driver+18+for+SQL+Server" is the URL-encoded driver name;
#   install "ODBC Driver 18 for SQL Server" from Microsoft if missing.
# - TrustServerCertificate=yes is needed for local dev because
#   Driver 18 encrypts by default and a local SQL Server usually
#   has a self-signed certificate.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=
